## 19. Risks and Mitigations

| Risk | Potential Impact | Initial Mitigation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| AI produces vague or overwhelming steps | Reduced trust and task initiation | Constrain output, offer editing, evaluate suggestions, and provide fallbacks |
| Recovery prompts feel judgmental | Users disengage | Use neutral language and test with target users |
| Excessive visual rewards cause sensory overload | Product conflicts with its core promise | Default to calm feedback and provide controls |
| Sensitive personal data is over-collected | Privacy and trust harm | Minimize collection and provide transparent controls |
| MVP scope becomes too broad | Core experience remains unfinished | Prioritize start, recover, return, and complete flows |
| AI latency or service failure blocks progress | User cannot continue | Provide loading, retry, manual-entry, and non-AI fallback states |
| Insights are mistaken for diagnosis | User harm and product liability | Use descriptive language and explicit non-medical boundaries |

